*
* START-HISTORY:
* 23 Oct 26 dm  Solo carry 15: Solo has ONE account, so the Accounts box is one row, the AI gate (set.ai gate on | off, the helper's own setting - Core's is a Linux group per
*               account, modify.account NAME ai-on), read from the helper's status instead of the register ($tk_gates is Core's and Solo has no such table).  Nothing else differs.
* 23 Oct 26 dm  (Core) New.
* 10 Nov 26 dm  SOLO CARRY (S.117): Core's shared frame, as every Core page has it: Esc and the menu bar, Ctrl-T, Ctrl-K, Ctrl-O and View > Mouse
*               ($tk_std), F6 / Shift-F6 between the boxes and the AI line ($tk_aipage, offered only refresh).  The page's own content is Solo's, unchanged.
* 11 Nov 26 dm  Carried from SD Core (S.160, 7 Nov 26, 74cf7001; the box's wording as Core has it since 8 Nov): T (and Provider > Standing text) opens the standing text -
*               the text sent first with every AI request - in a box with an editor: Save, Shipped default, Cancel; SET.AI CONTEXT keeps it.  T is not on the key row.
*               (Core's S.209, the page following a resize while the box is open, was not carried then; it is now, 12 Nov 26 below.)
* 11 Nov 26 dm  Carried from SD Core (owner, 11 Nov 2026: "Carry Core's dialog"): GOOGLE IS A ROW and every named provider has a DEFAULT model (Core e1061f73): five
*               provider rows, so the Provider box is one row taller and the Account box one row shorter (it has one account; five rows are shown); the table, the summary and
*               the detail show the model that will be asked, a default marked (default).  S IS THE SETUP DIALOG (Core S.170 / S.171, 2cced06c and d208d412): the key in a
*               password entry (a key already set shows as stars that keep it), the model chosen from the provider's own list (asked with the key when the dialog opens,
*               and again as soon as a new key is taken), Other name for a model no list holds.  The key is handed to the helper by file (SET.AI KEY p HANDOVER, in
*               $aikey of the Solo tree, a directory of mode 0700).  K and M are gone.  SET.AI KEY p at the prompt still keeps a key out of SD altogether.
* 12 Nov 26 dm  S.221 (Core-Solo parity audit, finding 7; owner, 12 Nov 2026: "Carry it"), SD Core's S.88 L2 and S.209: the four boxes are panes of the layout service
*               ($tk_layout) - drawn exactly as before at 140 by 43, and in a larger window the account box takes the extra rows and every box the extra columns; a resize is
*               followed, and a resize while the setup box or the standing-text box is open lays the page out again behind the box (after.box, box.resized).  The
*               Provider and Account boxes are named as focus boxes for $tk_frame's marks, as in Core.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.AI
*
*   For the administrator only (it is refused, before anything is read, for anyone else).  A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43
*   lines at least), with two boxes:
*
*     Provider   Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek and Custom, one to a row, with a check box on the provider in use (none marked: the AI is off), its address, its model and
*                whether its key is set.  The four named providers come with their connection details and a default model; the key is the administrator's, and so is any other
*                model (S).  Custom is the fifth choice, where the administrator fills in everything.  The row under the cursor is described in full below.
*     Account    The one Solo account, with the state of its ai gate (set.ai gate on | off): only while the gate is on can anything be sent to the provider.
*
*   Keys: Up and Down move, F6 or Left and Right change box, Enter selects or deselects the provider (Provider) or turns the gate on or off (Account), S the setup dialog (the key and the model, the model chosen from the provider's own list), X clears the key,
*   C fills in Custom, D removes it, A the file of certificate authorities, L a limit, T the standing text sent with every request, F5 reads the machine again, F1 or ? or a click on a [?] explains the
*   box, Ctrl-Q leaves.
*
*   THE PAGE KEEPS NO SETTING ITSELF.  What it shows it reads from the AI helper (KERNEL(K$AI.STATUS): the connection details, the models, whether a key is set,
*   the gate, the limits - never a key).  Every change is a SET.AI sentence shown with its effect in a box answered
*   Run or Cancel (Cancel is what Enter chooses) and run by $tk_runx; selecting a provider, turning the gate on, a certificate file and Custom ask for a
*   name to be typed, as turning on any switch that reaches beyond SD does.  THE KEY IS TYPED IN THE SETUP DIALOG (S), in a password entry, and handed to the helper
*   at once through a hand-over file (SET.AI KEY p HANDOVER), so it passes through this session; it is never shown, never on a command line and never in the audit
*   trail.  SET.AI KEY p at the prompt keeps a key out of SD altogether.  Nothing is turned on by opening the page.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_ai
$catalog $tool_ai

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   prompt ''

   allow.set = 'set.ai'                                        ;* the one command this page may run: SET.AI (through $tk_runx, which lets a word hold what SET.AI itself allows)
   okc = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._:/@+,-'          ;* the characters SET.AI allows in a word

   call $tk_open('tool.ai', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.ai')
   gosub lay.declare

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'enter', 'change', 'change', '', 1)
   * Core S.170 / S.171: S is the one setup dialog (the key and the model); K and M are gone
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 's', 'setup', 'setup', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'x', 'clear key', 'clearkey', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'c', 'custom', 'custom', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'drop custom', 'dropcustom', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'a', 'ca file', 'ca', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'l', 'limit', 'limit', 'Provider', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 't', 'standing text', 'context', '', 1)      ;* the text sent with every request, in a box (either box has it)
   keys<dcount(keys, @fm), TK.K.ROW> = 0                                   ;* bound and in the Provider menu, NOT on the key row (as in Core, whose row was full)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'refresh', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* Esc opens the menu bar, as on every page
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'change', '&Setting', '&Change the setting', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'setup', '&Provider', '&Key and model (setup)', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'clearkey', '&Provider', 'C&lear the key', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'custom', '&Provider', 'C&ustom provider', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'dropcustom', '&Provider', '&Drop the custom provider', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'ca', '&Provider', 'C&A file', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'limit', '&Provider', 'L&imit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'context', '&Provider', 'S&tanding text', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this box', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')  ;* the AI line is offered only refresh: no change of a setting is proposed by it
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)
   if aout then gosub lay.declare                         ;* the AI line took the body's last row: the panes again (as SD Core's pages)

   provs ='anthropic' : @fm : 'openai' : @fm : 'google' : @fm : 'deepseek' : @fm : 'custom'
   nprov = dcount(provs, @fm)                                  ;* the rows of the Provider box; the last is Custom
   lnames = 'requests-hour' : @fm : 'tokens-day' : @fm : 'timeout' : @fm : 'bytes-request' : @fm : 'bytes-reply' : @fm : 'max-tokens'
   pnames = 'Provider' : @fm : 'Account'

   pane = 1                                                    ;* (VISA, the account rows on the screen, is the layout's: lay.get; 5 at 140 by 43, and Solo has one account)
   pi = 1                                                      ;* the provider row under the cursor
   ci = 1                                                      ;* the account row under the cursor
   ta = 0                                                      ;* the account rows scrolled off the top
   gen = 0
   msg = 'Enter selects the provider with the check box; S sets up its key and model'
   done = 0

   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, '', '', mr)            ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, ao)           ;* while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, nm, 0, mr)       ;* F10, Alt and a letter, and Esc: the bar
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', lay.chg)
            gosub lay.get
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the machine says

* The helper's status line (never a key), and the state of the one account's ai gate (the helper's own setting)
read.all:
   helper.ok = 0
   hj = ''
   reply = kernel(K$AI.STATUS, 0)
   if reply<1> = 'D' then
      hj = jparse(reply<2>)
      if not(status()) and hj{'t'} = 'status' then helper.ok = 1
   end
   sel = ''
   pnm = '' ; purl = '' ; pfmt = '' ; paut = '' ; pver = '' ; pmax = '' ; pmod = '' ; pdef = '' ; pkey = ''
   ca = ''
   lim = ''
   if helper.ok then
      sel = hj{'provider'}
      for i = 1 to nprov
         p = provs<i>
         pnm<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/name'}
         purl<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/url'}
         pfmt<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/format'}
         paut<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/auth'}
         pver<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/version'}
         pmax<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/maxparam'}
         pmod<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/model'}                 ;* the model set, or null
         pdef<i> = hj{'providers/' : p : '/default'}               ;* the provider's starting model (null for Custom): used while pmod is null
         pkey<i> = (if hj{'providers/' : p : '/key'} then 1 else 0)
      next i
      ca = hj{'ca-file'}
      for i = 1 to dcount(lnames, @fm)
         lim<i> = hj{'limits/' : lnames<i>}
      next i
   end
   gosub read.accounts
   return

* Solo has one account: one row, its gate read from the helper's status (when the helper cannot be reached the gate shows as off and nothing can be changed)
read.accounts:
   an = 1
   anm = 'this account' ; auser = env('USER') ; ast = 0 ; asusp = 0
   if helper.ok then
      if hj{'gate'} then ast = 1                       ;* (no short-circuit in SD BASIC: the status is only asked of when it was read)
   end
   ci = 1
   return

* The page's four boxes as panes of $tk_layout (SD Core's S.88 L2, carried 12 Nov 26): each size is the box drawn at 140 by 43 (the body is 138 by 39; the boxes add up to 38,
* so that the last row, the AI line's, is free), so at that size nothing moves; in a larger window the account box stretches and every pane is as wide as the body.
lay.declare:
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'providers' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 10 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<2> = 'row' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 13 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<3> = 'accounts' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 9 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<4> = 'effect' : @vm : 4 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 6 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   ctx<TK.C.FOCI> = 'providers' : @sm : 'Provider' : @vm : 'accounts' : @sm : 'Account'        ;* the boxes that take the focus, for $tk_frame's [*] / [-] (pnames)
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, lay.err)
   gosub lay.get
   return

* The rectangles of the four panes, and what is counted from them: tw the width of a text line inside a box (134 at 140 by 43), VISA the account rows, DV the detail rows,
* EV the explanation rows
lay.get:
   lay.id = 'providers'
   gosub lay.rect
   pr.x = lay.x ; pr.y = lay.y ; pr.w = lay.w ; pr.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'row'
   gosub lay.rect
   dt.x = lay.x ; dt.y = lay.y ; dt.w = lay.w ; dt.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'accounts'
   gosub lay.rect
   ac.x = lay.x ; ac.y = lay.y ; ac.w = lay.w ; ac.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'effect'
   gosub lay.rect
   ef.x = lay.x ; ef.y = lay.y ; ef.w = lay.w ; ef.h = lay.h
   tx = pr.x + 2
   tw = pr.w - 4
   mk.px = pr.x + pr.w - 5                                      ;* the [?] button of each of the two boxes that have one, at the right end of its first row
   mk.py = pr.y + 1
   mk.ax = ac.x + ac.w - 5
   mk.ay = ac.y + 1
   VISA = ac.h - 4
   DV = dt.h - 2
   EV = ef.h - 2
   return

lay.rect:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, lay.id, lay.r)
   lay.x = lay.r<1, 1>
   lay.y = lay.r<1, 2>
   lay.w = lay.r<1, 3>
   lay.h = lay.r<1, 4>
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

draw.all:
   cw = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,1 size cw,chh
   screen box at pr.x,pr.y size pr.w,pr.h title 'AI provider'
   screen box at dt.x,dt.y size dt.w,dt.h title 'The row under the cursor'
   screen box at ac.x,ac.y size ac.w,ac.h title 'May this account use the AI?'
   screen box at ef.x,ef.y size ef.w,ef.h title 'What this means'
   gosub draw.providers
   gosub draw.detail
   gosub draw.accounts
   gosub draw.effect
   return

draw.providers:
   screen text '    ' : fmt('Provider', '14L') : fmt('Address', '56L') : fmt('Model', '28L') : 'Key' at tx,pr.y + 1 attr 'header' width tw
   for r = 1 to nprov
      s = ''
      if helper.ok then
         nm.s = pnm<r>
         if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
         url.s = purl<r>
         if url.s = '' then url.s = '(not filled in)'
         if len(url.s) > 54 then url.s = url.s[1, 52] : '..'
         gosub model.text
         s = '[' : (if provs<r> = sel then 'x' else ' ') : '] ' : fmt(nm.s, '14L') : fmt(url.s, '56L') : fmt(mod.s[1, 27], '28L') : (if pkey<r> then 'set' else 'not set')
      end
      screen text s at tx,pr.y + 1 + r attr (if r = pi then (if pane = 1 then 'highlight' else 'bold') else 'normal') width tw
   next r
   if not(helper.ok) then
      s = 'The AI helper is not running, or it is not installed: nothing here can be read or changed.'
   end else
      if sel = '' then
         s = 'The AI is OFF: no provider is selected.  Check a provider, give it its key (the model has a default), and turn the ai gate on.'
      end else
         lpid = sel
         gosub locate.prov
         k = lpr
         r = k
         gosub model.text
         s = 'In use: ' : pnm<k> : ', model ' : mod.s : ', key ' : (if pkey<k> then 'set' else 'not set')
         nomod = (pmod<k> = '' and pdef<k> = '')
         begin case
            case nomod and not(pkey<k>)
               s := '.  It cannot be used until both are set'
            case nomod
               s := '.  It cannot be used until a model is set'
            case not(pkey<k>)
               s := '.  It cannot be used until the key is set'
         end case
      end
   end
   screen text s at tx,pr.y + 8 attr 'bold' width tw
   call $tk_help('mark', mk.px, mk.py, 0, 0)
   return

* The row under the cursor, in full
draw.detail:
   lines = ''
   r = pi
   if not(helper.ok) then
      lines<-1> = 'No answer from the AI helper (the program sd-ai, started by your systemd user manager on the socket sd-solo-ai.sock in your runtime directory).'
   end else
      nm.s = pnm<r>
      if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
      if purl<r> = '' then
         lines<-1> = fmt('Name', '19L') : nm.s
         lines<-1> = fmt('Address', '19L') : '(not filled in)'
         lines<-1> = ''
         lines<-1> = "Custom is yours to fill in.  Press C and give the name, the https address, the request layout, the authentication, the version header and the name of the field that limits an answer's length."
         lines<-1> = ''
      end else
         lines<-1> = fmt('Name', '19L') : nm.s
         lines<-1> = fmt('Address', '19L') : purl<r>
         lines<-1> = fmt('Request layout', '19L') : pfmt<r> : (if pfmt<r> = 'anthropic' then '  (the Messages API)' else '  (chat completions)')
         lines<-1> = fmt('Authentication', '19L') : (if paut<r> = 'bearer' then 'Authorization: Bearer <key>' else 'x-api-key: <key>')
         lines<-1> = fmt('Version header', '19L') : (if pver<r> = '' then '(none)' else pver<r>)
         lines<-1> = fmt('Answer limit field', '19L') : pmax<r>
      end
      begin case
         case pmod<r> # ''
            lines<-1> = fmt('Model', '19L') : pmod<r> : (if pdef<r> = '' then '' else '  (yours; the default is ' : pdef<r> : ')')
         case pdef<r> # ''
            lines<-1> = fmt('Model', '19L') : pdef<r> : '  (the default that comes with SD; press S to choose another)'
         case 1
            lines<-1> = fmt('Model', '19L') : '(not set - press S)'
      end case
      lines<-1> = fmt('Key', '19L') : (if pkey<r> then 'set (kept for the AI helper only; this page never shows it)' else 'not set - press S')
      lines<-1> = ''
      lines<-1> = 'Certificate authorities: ' : (if ca = '' then 'the system store' else ca)
      s = ''
      for i = 1 to dcount(lnames, @fm)
         s := lnames<i> : ' ' : lim<i> : (if i < dcount(lnames, @fm) then ', ' else '')
      next i
      lines<-1> = 'Limits: ' : s
   end
   gosub wrap.lines
   for r = 1 to DV
      screen text fmt(lines<r>, tw : 'L') at dt.x + 2,dt.y + r width tw
   next r
   return

draw.accounts:
   screen text fmt('Account', '24L') : fmt('Linux user', '24L') : 'AI gate' at ac.x + 2,ac.y + 1 attr 'header' width tw      ;* (one row in Solo)
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VISA then ta = ci - VISA
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VISA
      k = ta + r
      s = ''
      if k <= an then
         s = fmt(anm<k>, '24L') : fmt(auser<k>, '24L') : (if ast<k> = 1 then 'ON ' else 'off') : (if asusp<k> then '   (suspended)' else '')
      end
      screen text s at ac.x + 2,ac.y + 1 + r attr (if k = ci and k <= an then (if pane = 2 then 'highlight' else 'bold') else 'normal') width tw
   next r
   if ast = 1 then
      s = 'The gate is ON: this account can send text to the provider.  Enter turns the gate off.'
   end else
      s = 'The gate is off (as delivered): nothing can be sent to the provider.  Enter turns the gate on.'
   end
   screen text s at ac.x + 2,ac.y + ac.h - 2 attr 'bold' width tw          ;* the account box's last row (31 at 140 by 43)
   call $tk_help('mark', mk.ax, mk.ay, 0, 0)
   return

* In plain sentences
draw.effect:
   lines = ''
   lines<-1> = 'One provider and one model serve the account.  The AI is off as delivered: it needs a provider, its key (a default model comes with each named provider) and the ai gate turned on.'
   lines<-1> = "S sets up the provider under the cursor: the key (shown as *) and the model, chosen from the provider's own list; the key is kept for the AI helper only and this page never shows it (set.ai key at the prompt keeps it out of SD altogether).  What the account sends leaves this machine for the provider checked above, over https with the certificate checked."
   if pane = 1 then
      p = provs<pi>
      if p = sel then
         lines<-1> = 'Selected: ' : (if pnm<pi> = '' then 'Custom' else pnm<pi>) : ' is the provider in use.  Enter stops using it, which turns the AI off.'
      end else
         lines<-1> = 'Selected: ' : (if pnm<pi> = '' then 'Custom' else pnm<pi>) : ' is not in use.  Enter makes it the provider in use (you type its name to confirm).'
      end
   end else
      lines<-1> = 'Selected: ' : anm<ci> : (if ast = 1 then ' may use the AI.  Enter turns that off (at the next request).' else ' may not use the AI.  Enter turns it on (you type ai to confirm; at the next request).')
   end
   gosub wrap.lines
   for r = 1 to EV
      screen text fmt(lines<r>, tw : 'L') at ef.x + 2,ef.y + r width tw
   next r
   return

* A SCREEN TEXT longer than its width is cut, not wrapped
wrap.lines:
   wrapped = ''
   for wi = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
      if lines<wi> = '' then
         wrapped<-1> = ''
      end else
         call $tk_wrap(lines<wi>, tw, pieces)
         wrapped<-1> = pieces
      end
   next wi
   lines = wrapped
   return

* A row of the Provider box: the model it will ask, for the table and the summary.  In: r.  Out: mod.s - the model set, else the provider's default with (default)
* after it, else (not set)
model.text:
   mod.s = pmod<r>
   if mod.s = '' then
      mod.s = pdef<r>
      if mod.s = '' then mod.s = '(not set)' else mod.s := ' (default)'
   end
   return

* The row of the provider whose id is in lpid (1 when it is none of them)
locate.prov:
   lpr = 1
   for lp2 = 1 to nprov
      if provs<lp2> = lpid then lpr = lp2
   next lp2
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 and nm >= 'A' and nm <= 'Z' then nm = downcase(nm)
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         if pane = 1 and pi > 1 then
            pi -= 1
            gosub redraw
         end
         if pane = 2 and ci > 1 then
            ci -= 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'down'
         if pane = 1 and pi < nprov then
            pi += 1
            gosub redraw
         end
         if pane = 2 and ci < an then
            ci += 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'right' or nm = 'left'                       ;* S.176 in Core: F6 / Shift-F6 change the box, Tab no longer does (Left and Right still do)
         pane = (if pane = 1 then 2 else 1)
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'enter' or nm = ' '
         if pane = 1 then gosub select.provider else gosub toggle.gate
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         gosub help.here
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read the machine again'
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, std.r)
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, pane, nm : @fm : 2, ap)         ;* F6 / Shift-F6 go round the two boxes and the AI line; AI > Ask the AI goes to the line
         if ap<1> > 0 and ap<1> # pane then
            pane = ap<1>
            gosub draw.all
         end
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
      case nm = 't'
         if helper.ok then gosub do.context else msg = sysmsg(11607)
      case nm = 's' or nm = 'x' or nm = 'c' or nm = 'd' or nm = 'a' or nm = 'l'
         if pane # 1 then
            msg = 'Move to the Provider box (Tab) for that key'
         end else
            if not(helper.ok) then
               msg = sysmsg(11607)                                ;* The AI helper could not be reached
            end else
               begin case
                  case nm = 's'
                     gosub do.setup
                  case nm = 'x'
                     gosub do.clearkey
                  case nm = 'c'
                     gosub do.custom
                  case nm = 'd'
                     gosub do.dropcustom
                  case nm = 'a'
                     gosub do.ca
                  case nm = 'l'
                     gosub do.limit
               end case
            end
         end
   end case
   return

redraw:
   gosub draw.providers
   gosub draw.detail
   gosub draw.accounts
   gosub draw.effect
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, mev, '', mr)                   ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, mev, ap)                          ;* a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, mk.px, mk.py, hit.prov)
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, mk.ax, mk.ay, hit.acc)
   if hit.prov or hit.acc then
      pane = (if hit.prov then 1 else 2)
      gosub redraw
      gosub help.here
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      begin case
         case mx >= pr.x + 1 and mx <= pr.x + pr.w - 2 and my >= pr.y + 2 and my <= pr.y + 1 + nprov
            pi = my - pr.y - 1
            pane = 1
            gosub redraw
         case mx >= ac.x + 1 and mx <= ac.x + ac.w - 2 and my >= ac.y + 2 and my <= ac.y + 1 + VISA
            if ta + my - ac.y - 1 <= an then ci = ta + my - ac.y - 1
            pane = 2
            gosub redraw
      end case
   end
   return

help.here:
   call $tk_help('box', (if pane = 1 then 'tool.ai.providers' else 'tool.ai.accounts'), hm, 0, 0)
   if hm # '' then msg = hm
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- changing something: the command, its effect, Run or Cancel, then the machine's answer

* Whether vw is a word SET.AI would take: 1 to vmax characters, all of okc
valid.word:
   vw.ok = (len(vw) >= 1 and len(vw) <= vmax)
   if vw.ok then
      if trim(convert(okc, space(len(okc)), vw)) # '' then vw.ok = 0
   end
   return

* The sentence in sent, its effect in el, the name to be typed in typed (null for Run / Cancel); every sentence is a SET.AI one (the wider word set of $tk_runx)
confirm.and.run:
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res = 'run' then
      call $tk_runx(allow.set, sent, out, st, err)
      if err # '' then
         msg = err
      end else
         said = trim(change(out, @fm, ' '))
         msg = (if said # '' then said[1, 130] else 'ran, status ' : st)
      end
      gosub read.all
      gosub draw.all
   end else
      msg = cmsg
   end
   return

* Enter on a provider: check it (the one in use), or uncheck the one in use (the AI is then off)
select.provider:
   if not(helper.ok) then
      msg = sysmsg(11607)
      return
   end
   p = provs<pi>
   nm.s = pnm<pi>
   if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
   el = ''
   if p = sel then
      sent = 'set.ai provider none'
      typed = ''
      el<-1> = 'The AI will be off: no provider will be selected.'
      el<-1> = 'The model, the key and the ai gate stay as they are.'
   end else
      sent = 'set.ai provider ' : p
      typed = p
      el<-1> = 'From now on, while the ai gate is on, ' : nm.s : ' will be used.'
      host = field(purl<pi>, '/', 3)
      if host # '' then el<-1> = 'The text they send leaves this machine for ' : host : ' over https.'
      if pmod<pi> = '' and pdef<pi> = '' then el<-1> = 'No model is set for it yet, so it cannot be used until you press S.'
      if pmod<pi> = '' and pdef<pi> # '' then el<-1> = 'It will ask its default model, ' : pdef<pi> : ' (S chooses another).'
      if not(pkey<pi>) then el<-1> = 'No key is set for it yet, so it cannot be used until you press S.'
      if p = 'custom' and purl<pi> = '' then el<-1> = 'Custom is not filled in yet: press C first (the helper refuses it until then).'
   end
   el<-1> = 'It takes effect at once.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* Enter on the account: its ai gate, on or off
toggle.gate:
   if not(helper.ok) then
      msg = sysmsg(11607)
      return
   end
   on.now = (ast = 1)
   sent = 'set.ai gate ' : (if on.now then 'off' else 'on')
   el = ''
   typed = ''
   if on.now then
      el<-1> = 'This account will no longer be able to send anything to the AI.  Nothing else changes: the provider, model and key stay.'
   end else
      typed = 'ai'
      lpid = sel
      gosub locate.prov
      k = lpr
      if sel # '' then
         el<-1> = 'This account will be able to send text to ' : (if pnm<k> = '' then 'Custom' else pnm<k>) : ' with the ai verb and the programs that ask the AI.  The text leaves this machine.'
      end else
         el<-1> = 'This account will be able to use the AI as soon as you choose a provider.  What it sends leaves this machine for that provider.'
      end
      el<-1> = 'Solo runs the AI helper as you, so any program of yours can use the key the helper holds; the gate is the one switch SD keeps.'
   end
   el<-1> = 'It takes effect at the next request to the AI: the helper looks at the setting each time.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* S (Core S.170 / S.171; the owner, 8 Nov 26: first "a single dialog with the key field displaying asterisks", then: "There should be only S for a setup dialog that looks the
* same no matter if the model and key has been selected previously.  If there are already values they should be displayed.  The model should be selected from a list.  The key
* in a password type field."  Warned that the key then passes through SD, he chose this over the helper's own prompt; carried to Solo on his "Carry Core's dialog", 11 Nov 26.)
* ONE DIALOG, ALWAYS THE SAME: the Key (a password entry: a key already set shows as SU.KEEP, the stars that mean "keep it"), the Model (a LIST of the provider's own model
* names, the one in use chosen), Other name (an entry for a model no list holds: a Custom server that gives no list), three message rows, Save and Cancel.  The list is asked for
* when the dialog opens if a key is set, and again as soon as a new key is taken (leaving the Key entry, or Enter in it): the key goes to the helper first (SET.AI KEY p HANDOVER,
* through a file in a directory of mode 0700 in the Solo tree, removed at once; never a command line or the audit trail), then the list is asked WITH it.  Save sets the model
* chosen when it differs from the one in use.  The model now set that the list does not hold is said, and the listed one that differs only in case is chosen.
do.setup:
   p = provs<pi>
   if index(' anthropic openai google deepseek custom ', ' ' : p : ' ', 1) = 0 then return
   nm.s = pnm<pi>
   if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
   cur = pmod<pi>
   if cur = '' then cur = pdef<pi>
   host = field(purl<pi>, '/', 3)
   if host = '' then
      msg = nm.s : ' has no address yet: fill it in first (press C)'
      return
   end
   su.keep = '************'
   call $sl_scr('get', scr)
   su.sw = scr<SL.S.W> + 0
   su.sh = scr<SL.S.H> + 0
   su.bw = 100
   su.bh = 28
   if su.sw < su.bw + 2 or su.sh < su.bh + 2 then
      msg = 'the window is too small for the setup dialog: nothing was changed'
      return
   end
   su.bx = int((su.sw - su.bw) / 2)
   su.by = int((su.sh - su.bh) / 2)
   su.lw = 14
   su.mw = su.bw - 4
   key.done = 0
   lm.ok = 0 ; lm.n = 0 ; lm.list = '' ; lm.why = ''
   if pkey<pi> then gosub fetch.models
   gosub setup.items
   su.title = 'AI setup: ' : nm.s
   if pkey<pi> then
      su.kini = su.keep
      su.khint = 'A key is set.  Leave the stars to keep it, or replace them with a new key.'
   end else
      su.kini = ''
      su.khint = 'Type or paste the key, then press Tab: the list of models is fetched with it.'
   end
   su.hint = ('The key is sent only to ' : host : ' over https.  Tab moves, Enter saves, Esc cancels.')[1, su.mw]
   su.tw = su.bw - su.lw - 4
   screen form title su.title at su.bx,su.by size su.bw,su.bh returning sf
   screen label sf, 'lk', 'Key' at 2,2 width su.lw - 2
   screen entry sf, 'key' at 2 + su.lw,2 width 70 value su.kini mask maxlen 600
   screen label sf, 'lk2', su.khint at 2 + su.lw,3 width su.tw
   screen label sf, 'lm', 'Model' at 2,5 width su.lw - 2
   screen list sf, 'model', su.items at 2 + su.lw,5 size 70,12 value su.val
   screen label sf, 'lo', 'Other name' at 2,18 width su.lw - 2
   screen entry sf, 'other' at 2 + su.lw,18 width 50 value '' maxlen 80
   screen label sf, 'lo2', 'Only for a model the list does not hold (a Custom server that gives no list).' at 2 + su.lw,19 width su.tw
   for j = 1 to 3
      screen label sf, 'm' : j, '' at 2,20 + j width su.mw
   next j
   screen button sf, 'ok', '&Save' at 2,su.bh - 3 default
   screen button sf, 'cancel', sysmsg(11249) at 14,su.bh - 3 cancel
   screen label sf, 'hint', su.hint at 2,su.bh - 2 width su.mw
   su.say = su.note
   gosub setup.say
   su.done = 0
   loop
      screen wait sf returning su.ev then                     ;* su.ev, NOT ev: names fold case, and EV is the page's explanation rows
         begin case
            case su.ev<1> = 'resize'                          ;* S.209: the box goes, the page follows the window, and the next wait shows the box over it
               screen hide sf
               gosub box.resized
            case su.ev<1> = 'focus'
               if su.ev<3> = 'key' then gosub setup.takekey   ;* the Key entry was left: a new key in it goes to the helper and the list is asked with it
            case su.ev<1> = 'button' and su.ev<2> = 'ok'
               gosub setup.takekey                            ;* Enter in the Key entry presses Save: take a new key first
               if not(su.fetched) then gosub setup.save        ;* a list that has only just come is shown to choose from, not saved over
            case su.ev<1> = 'button'
               exit
         end case
      end else
         exit                                                 ;* Esc, Cancel, an input that ended
      end
      if su.done then exit
   repeat
   kv = ''
   screen hide sf
   gosub after.box
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   if su.done then
      msg = (if key.done then 'The key for ' : nm.s : ' is set' else 'The key is unchanged')
      if mv # cur then                                         ;* cur is the model in use (the one set, else the default)
         call $tk_runx(allow.set, 'set.ai model ' : p : ' ' : mv, out, st, err)
         if err # '' then
            msg := '; the model was not set: ' : err
         end else
            msg := '; ' : trim(change(out, @fm, ' '))[1, 100]
         end
      end else
         msg := '; the model stays ' : mv
      end
   end else
      msg = (if key.done then 'the key is set; the model was not changed' else 'nothing was changed')
   end
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   return

* The dialog's model list from lm.* (su.items, values), the entry to start on (su.val) and what the message rows say (su.note): the model in use chosen; one the list does not hold
* said, with the listed one that differs only in case chosen; no list yet (no key) or none from the provider said in the list's one row.
setup.items:
   su.items = ''
   su.val = 1
   su.note = ''
   if lm.ok and lm.n > 0 then
      su.items = change(lm.list, @fm, @vm)
      found = 0
      near = 0
      for i = 1 to lm.n
         if lm.list<i> = cur then
            su.val = i
            found = 1
         end
         if near = 0 and downcase(lm.list<i>) = downcase(cur) then near = i
      next i
      begin case
         case found
            su.note = nm.s : ' lists ' : lm.n : ' models; the one in use, ' : cur : ', is chosen.'
         case near
            su.val = near
            su.note = 'The model now set, ' : cur : ', is not in ' : nm.s : "'s list (model names are case-sensitive).  " : lm.list<near> : ' is chosen: Save to use it.'
         case cur # ''
            su.note = 'The model now set, ' : cur : ', is not in ' : nm.s : "'s list.  Choose one and Save."
         case 1
            su.note = nm.s : ' lists ' : lm.n : ' models.  Choose one and Save.'
      end case
   end else
      if pkey<pi> or key.done then
         su.items = '(no list from ' : nm.s : ')'
         su.note = nm.s : ' gave no list of models' : (if lm.why # '' then ': ' : lm.why else '') : '.  Type the model under Other name.'
      end else
         su.items = '(set the key first: the list comes from ' : nm.s : ')'
         su.note = 'No key is set for ' : nm.s : ' yet.  Type or paste it, then press Tab.'
      end
   end
   return

* The message rows of the dialog: su.say, wrapped
setup.say:
   call $tk_wrap(su.say, su.mw, pieces)
   for j = 1 to 3
      screen set sf, 'm' : j text pieces<j>[1, su.mw]
   next j
   return

* A new key in the Key entry (anything but the keep-stars or nothing) goes to the helper, then the list is asked with it and shown.  su.fetched is 1 when that happened.  The
* entry shows the keep-stars again afterwards; kv is cleared on every path.
setup.takekey:
   su.fetched = 0
   screen get sf, 'key' returning kv
   kv = trim(kv)
   if kv = su.keep or kv = '' then
      kv = ''
      return
   end
   if kv[1, len(su.keep)] = su.keep then kv = kv[len(su.keep) + 1, 9999]    ;* typed after the stars without clearing them
   gosub key.word
   if not(kw.ok) then
      kv = ''
      su.say = 'A key is 8 to 512 characters with no space and nothing outside plain ASCII.  Nothing was set.'
      gosub setup.say
      screen focus sf, 'key' else null
      return
   end
   gosub hand.key                                             ;* kv is cleared there, whatever happens
   if hk.err # '' then
      su.say = 'The key was not set: ' : hk.err
      gosub setup.say
      screen focus sf, 'key' else null
      return
   end
   key.done = 1
   screen set sf, 'key' value su.keep
   gosub fetch.models
   gosub setup.items
   screen set sf, 'model' items su.items
   screen set sf, 'model' value su.val
   su.say = 'The key for ' : nm.s : ' is set.  ' : su.note
   gosub setup.say
   if lm.ok and lm.n > 0 then
      screen focus sf, 'model' else null
   end
   su.fetched = 1
   return

* Save: the model from Other name when it is filled in (checked against the list when there is one), else the one chosen in the list.  su.done 1 and mv when it may be set.
setup.save:
   su.done = 0
   if not(pkey<pi>) and not(key.done) then
      su.say = 'No key is set for ' : nm.s : ': type or paste it first.'
      gosub setup.say
      screen focus sf, 'key' else null
      return
   end
   screen get sf, 'other' returning ov
   ov = trim(ov)
   if ov # '' then
      vw = ov
      vmax = 80
      gosub valid.word
      if not(vw.ok) then
         su.say = 'A model name has 1 to 80 letters, digits and . _ : / @ + , - and nothing else.'
         gosub setup.say
         screen focus sf, 'other' else null
         return
      end
      if lm.ok and lm.n > 0 then
         found = 0
         near = ''
         for i = 1 to lm.n
            if lm.list<i> = ov then found = 1
            if near = '' and downcase(lm.list<i>) = downcase(ov) then near = lm.list<i>
         next i
         if not(found) then
            su.say = nm.s : ' does not list a model named ' : ov : '.' : (if near # '' then '  It lists ' : near : ' (model names are case-sensitive).' else '  Choose one from the list.')
            gosub setup.say
            screen focus sf, 'other' else null
            return
         end
      end
      mv = ov
   end else
      if not(lm.ok and lm.n > 0) then
         su.say = 'There is no list to choose from: type the model under Other name.'
         gosub setup.say
         screen focus sf, 'other' else null
         return
      end
      screen get sf, 'model' returning li
      li = li + 0
      if li < 1 or li > lm.n then li = 1
      mv = lm.list<li>
   end
   su.done = 1
   return

* kw.ok 1 when kv is a word the helper takes as a key: 8 to 512 characters from ! to ~
key.word:
   kw.ok = (len(kv) >= 8 and len(kv) <= 512)
   if kw.ok then
      for kw.i = 1 to len(kv)
         kw.c = seq(kv[kw.i, 1])
         if kw.c < 33 or kw.c > 126 then
            kw.ok = 0
            exit
         end
      next kw.i
   end
   return

* The key in kv to the helper, through the hand-over file SET.AI KEY p HANDOVER reads and removes.  The directory ($aikey in the Solo tree, @sdsys) is made 0700 (the Solo
* user's alone) before the file is written in it, and the file is removed here as well, whatever SET.AI did.  kv is cleared.  hk.err is null when the helper has the key,
* otherwise what went wrong.
hand.key:
   hk.err = ''
   hdir = @sdsys : @ds : '$aikey'
   hf = hdir : @ds : 'key'
   os.execute "umask 077; mkdir -p '" : hdir : "' && chmod 700 '" : hdir : "' && rm -f '" : hf : "'"
   openseq hf to kf else
      if status() then
         hk.err = 'the hand-over file could not be made'
         kv = ''
         if not(unassigned(kf)) then close kf
         return
      end
   end
   writeseq kv to kf else hk.err = 'the hand-over file could not be written'
   close kf
   kv = ''
   if hk.err = '' then
      call $tk_runx(allow.set, 'set.ai key ' : p : ' handover', out, st, err)
      if err # '' then
         hk.err = err
      end else
         if st # 0 then hk.err = trim(change(out, @fm, ' '))[1, 100]
      end
   end
   os.execute "rm -f '" : hf : "'"
   return

* The provider's list of model names (p), asked through SET.AI MODELS: lm.ok 1 with lm.list (one to a field) and lm.n; lm.ok 0 when there is none (lm.why says why)
fetch.models:
   lm.ok = 0 ; lm.list = '' ; lm.n = 0 ; lm.why = ''
   call $tk_runx(allow.set, 'set.ai models ' : p, out, st, err)
   if err # '' then
      lm.why = err
      return
   end
   if st # 0 then
      lm.why = trim(change(out, @fm, ' '))[1, 120]
      return
   end
   lm.ok = 1
   for i = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
      if out<i>[1, 2] = '  ' and trim(out<i>) # '' then
         lm.n += 1
         lm.list<lm.n> = trim(out<i>)
      end
   next i
   return

* T (Core S.160; the owner, 7 Nov 26: "a standard text that will be included with every AI query describing where the default agent help text is located along any other
* information that will help the AI.  It can be accessed in a popup using a shortcut key on the AI selection pane.  It should be editable but supplied with the default
* text").  The text the helper keeps is shown in a box with an editor; Save puts it in place of the one in use, Shipped default takes the administrator's text away so that
* the default beside the helper is sent again.  The page checks the text as the helper and SET.AI will (printable ASCII and line feeds, 4000 characters) only to say so
* in the box; SET.AI CONTEXT decides, and puts it to the wall's screen.  THE SENTENCE IS RUN HERE, NOT BY $tk_runx: its one word is the text in hexadecimal, up to 8000
* characters, and $tk_runx takes 500.  The verb is fixed and the word is checked to be hexadecimal before it is run, so the sentence can hold nothing else.  The Run / Cancel
* box names the sentence with the word described, since the text itself was on the screen a moment before.
do.context:
   cx.cur = hj{'context'}
   cx.from = hj{'context-from'}
   call $sl_window(cx.scrw, cx.scrh)
   cx.w = cx.scrw - 8
   if cx.w > 120 then cx.w = 120
   cx.h = cx.scrh - 6
   if cx.h > 36 then cx.h = 36
   cx.x = int((cx.scrw - cx.w) / 2)
   cx.y = int((cx.scrh - cx.h) / 2)
   begin case
      case cx.from = 'own'
         cx.whose = "the administrator's own"
      case cx.from = 'default'
         cx.whose = 'the shipped default'
      case cx.from = 'bad'
         cx.whose = 'the kept text cannot be used, so none is sent'
      case 1
         cx.whose = 'none'
   end case
   screen form title 'Standing text sent with every AI request' at cx.x,cx.y size cx.w,cx.h returning cf
   screen label cf, 'l1', 'Sent first with every AI request; the person asking never sees it.  Now: ' : cx.whose : '.' at 2,1 width cx.w - 6
   screen label cf, 'l2', 'Plain English, 4000 characters at most.  Enter: new line.  Tab: the buttons.  Kept only after Save and Run.' at 2,2 width cx.w - 6
   screen memo cf, 'txt', convert(char(10), @fm, cx.cur) at 2,4 size cx.w - 6,cx.h - 10
   screen set cf, 'txt' wrap 1                                 ;* a long line is SHOWN on several rows; the text is not changed
   screen label cf, 'note', ' ' at 2,cx.h - 5 width cx.w - 6
   screen button cf, 'save', '&Save' at 2,cx.h - 3 default
   screen button cf, 'dflt', 'Shipped &default' at 14,cx.h - 3
   screen button cf, 'cancel', '&Cancel' at 36,cx.h - 3 cancel
   cx.act = ''
   loop
      screen wait cf returning cx.ev then                     ;* cx.ev, NOT ev: names fold case, and EV is the page's explanation rows
         if cx.ev<1> = 'resize' then                          ;* S.209: the box goes, the page follows the window, and the next wait shows the box over it
            screen hide cf
            gosub box.resized
         end
         if cx.ev<1> = 'button' then
            begin case
               case cx.ev<2> = 'cancel'
                  cx.act = 'cancel'
               case cx.ev<2> = 'dflt'
                  cx.act = 'default'
               case cx.ev<2> = 'save'
                  screen get cf, 'txt' returning cx.new
                  cx.new = trimb(convert(@fm, char(10), cx.new))
                  loop
                  while len(cx.new) > 0 and cx.new[len(cx.new), 1] = char(10) do
                     cx.new = cx.new[1, len(cx.new) - 1]
                  repeat
                  gosub context.check
                  if cx.bad # '' then
                     screen set cf, 'note' text cx.bad
                  end else
                     cx.act = 'save'
                  end
            end case
         end
      end else
         cx.act = 'cancel'                                     ;* Esc, or an input that ended
      end
   until cx.act # ''
   repeat
   screen hide cf
   gosub after.box
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub draw.all
   begin case
      case cx.act = 'cancel'
         msg = 'the standing text is unchanged'
         return
      case cx.act = 'default'
         if cx.from = 'default' then
            msg = 'the standing text is already the shipped default'
            return
         end
         cx.sent = 'set.ai context -'
         cx.show = cx.sent
         el = ''
         el<-1> = "The administrator's standing text is removed, and the default shipped with SD is sent with every AI request from now on."
      case 1
         if cx.new = cx.cur and cx.from # 'bad' then
            msg = 'the standing text is unchanged'
            return
         end
         cx.sent = 'set.ai context ' : oconv(cx.new, 'MX0C')
         cx.show = 'set.ai context <the text above, ' : len(cx.new) : ' characters, as hexadecimal>'
         el = ''
         el<-1> = 'Every AI request will begin with this text (' : len(cx.new) : ' characters); it is not shown in the preview.'
         el<-1> = 'A text that names SD' : "'" : 's own code or build is refused.'
   end case
   call $tk_confirm(cx.show, el, '', res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   if downcase(field(cx.sent, ' ', 1)) # 'set.ai' or field(cx.sent, ' ', 2) # 'context' or dcount(cx.sent, ' ') # 3 then return
   cx.word = field(cx.sent, ' ', 3)
   if cx.word # '-' and convert('0123456789ABCDEFabcdef', '', cx.word) # '' then return       ;* the one word is hexadecimal (or -) and nothing else
   execute cx.sent trapping aborts capturing out
   said = trim(change(out, @fm, ' '))
   msg = (if said # '' then said[1, 130] else 'ran, status ' : @system.return.code)
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   return

* S.209 (SD Core's, carried 12 Nov 26): the page's own boxes (the setup box and the standing text) run their own SCREEN WAIT, and a resize that comes while one is open is
*   taken by the box: the page never saw it and was drawn again at its old size.  So when a box closes the layout is asked again, which is the main loop's own resize step.
after.box:
   call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', lay.chg)
   gosub lay.get
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   return

* A resize while a box is open: the page is laid out and drawn at the new size behind it (the box was hidden first; its next SCREEN WAIT shows it again on top)
box.resized:
   gosub after.box
   gosub draw.all
   call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, '', '', mr)      ;* the bar and the foot too: the main loop that draws them is waiting for the box
   call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, pnames<pane>, msg)
   return

* In: cx.new.  Out: cx.bad, null when the helper would take it, else what is wrong (said in the box)
context.check:
   cx.bad = ''
   if cx.new = '' then
      cx.bad = 'The text is empty.  To send the default again, choose Shipped default.'
      return
   end
   if len(cx.new) > 4000 then
      cx.bad = 'The text has ' : len(cx.new) : ' characters; at most 4000 are kept.'
      return
   end
   for cx.i = 1 to len(cx.new)
      cx.c = seq(cx.new[cx.i, 1])
      if cx.c # 10 and (cx.c < 32 or cx.c > 126) then
         cx.bad = 'Character ' : cx.i : ' is not plain text (only printable ASCII and new lines are kept).'
         return
      end
   next cx.i
   return

* X: remove the key of the provider under the cursor
do.clearkey:
   p = provs<pi>
   nm.s = pnm<pi>
   if nm.s = '' then nm.s = 'Custom'
   if not(pkey<pi>) then
      msg = 'No key is set for ' : nm.s
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai key ' : p : ' clear'
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The key for ' : nm.s : ' will be removed from the AI helper.  The AI cannot be used with it until a key is set again (press S).'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* C: the Custom row, every field the administrator's
do.custom:
   if provs<pi> # 'custom' then
      msg = 'C fills in the Custom row: move the cursor to it first'
      return
   end
   v1 = (if purl<nprov> = '' then '' else pnm<nprov>)
   v2 = purl<nprov>
   v3 = pfmt<nprov>
   v4 = paut<nprov>
   v5 = pver<nprov>
   v6 = pmax<nprov>
   screen ask 'Name (letters, digits and . _ : / @ + , - only)' width 40 value v1 title 'Custom AI connection  1 of 6' returning v1 else return
   screen ask 'Address: https only, no query string' width 100 value v2 title 'Custom AI connection  2 of 6' returning v2 else return
   screen ask 'Request layout: anthropic or openai' width 12 value v3 title 'Custom AI connection  3 of 6' returning v3 else return
   screen ask 'Authentication: bearer or x-api-key' width 12 value v4 title 'Custom AI connection  4 of 6' returning v4 else return
   screen ask 'Version header (empty or a dash for none)' width 24 value v5 title 'Custom AI connection  5 of 6' returning v5 else return
   screen ask 'Field that limits the length of an answer (max_tokens or max_completion_tokens)' width 30 value v6 title 'Custom AI connection  6 of 6' returning v6 else return
   v1 = trim(v1) ; v2 = trim(v2) ; v3 = downcase(trim(v3)) ; v4 = downcase(trim(v4)) ; v5 = trim(v5) ; v6 = trim(v6)
   if v5 = '' then v5 = '-'
   bad = ''
   vmax = 40 ; vw = v1 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) then bad = 'the name'
   vmax = 300 ; vw = v2 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) or v2[1, 8] # 'https://' then bad = 'the address (https://, no query string)'
   if v3 # 'anthropic' and v3 # 'openai' then bad = 'the request layout (anthropic or openai)'
   if v4 # 'bearer' and v4 # 'x-api-key' then bad = 'the authentication (bearer or x-api-key)'
   vmax = 40 ; vw = v5 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) then bad = 'the version header'
   vmax = 60 ; vw = v6 ; gosub valid.word ; if not(vw.ok) then bad = 'the answer length field'
   if bad # '' then
      msg = 'Not accepted: ' : bad : '.  Nothing was changed'
      gosub draw.all
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai custom ' : v1 : ' ' : v2 : ' ' : v3 : ' ' : v4 : ' ' : v5 : ' ' : v6
   typed = 'custom'
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'Custom will go to ' : field(v2, '/', 3) : ' over https, with the certificate checked, and the key is sent only to that address.'
   el<-1> = 'The helper checks the address again.  It is not used until you check Custom and set its key and model (S).'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* D: forget the Custom connection
do.dropcustom:
   if provs<pi> # 'custom' then
      msg = 'D removes the Custom row: move the cursor to it first'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai custom clear'
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The Custom connection is removed.  The helper refuses this while Custom is the provider in use.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* A: the file of certificate authorities the helper trusts (instead of the system store); a dash is the system store
do.ca:
   screen ask 'File of certificate authorities for a private CA (a dash is the system store)' width 100 value ca title 'Certificate authorities' returning cv else return
   cv = trim(cv)
   vw = cv
   vmax = 300
   gosub valid.word
   if not(vw.ok) then
      msg = 'A file name here has letters, digits and . _ : / @ + , - and nothing else'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai ca ' : cv
   el = ''
   if cv = '-' then
      typed = ''
      el<-1> = 'The helper will trust the system store of certificate authorities only (the delivered state).'
   end else
      typed = 'ca'
      el<-1> = 'The helper will trust ONLY the authorities in ' : cv : ', not the system store.'
      el<-1> = 'Whoever holds a key of one of those authorities can read what accounts send and the AI key.  Use a file you trust.'
   end
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* L: one limit
do.limit:
   screen ask 'Limit (requests-hour, tokens-day, timeout, bytes-request, bytes-reply or max-tokens)' width 16 title 'AI limit' returning ln else return
   ln = downcase(trim(ln))
   locate ln in lnames<1> setting lk else
      msg = ln : ' is not one of the six limits'
      return
   end
   screen ask 'New value for ' : ln : ' (it is ' : lim<lk> : ' now; a whole number)' width 10 title 'AI limit' returning lv else return
   lv = trim(lv)
   if lv = '' or len(lv) > 9 or trim(convert('0123456789', space(10), lv)) # '' then
      msg = 'A limit is a whole number of up to 9 digits'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.ai limit ' : ln : ' ' : lv
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The limit ' : ln : ' will be ' : lv : ' (it is ' : lim<lk> : ' now).  The helper checks the range.'
   el<-1> = 'requests-hour and tokens-day count what each account sends; the other four cap one request.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

end

